  "primary": "All three rb1 Nov 16 gap_follow runs as one reserved date, irrespective of speed, duration, missing topics, or direction of effect. No replacements. Equal-weight mean of eligible runs’ wrapped steering MAE (learned minus original, rad); list each run and paired tick-weighted aggregate. Negative means closer imitation, not better driving. An empty run is reported and not imputed.",
  "secondary": "Same comparison to the fixed October gains. Report speed MAE, turn direction, safety interventions and stops; per car/date/publisher and measured-speed bucket; contextual Nov 9/11 kept separate. Compare original, October gains, frozen learned steering separately, no selector. No inferential generalization across dates on one reserved day.",
  "protocol": "PR94 exact alignment and history resets; each policy feeds back its own wrapped commands. Same causal scans, reactive mode, no map/preview/camera/IMU, per-car wrapper at fixed comparison cap. No safety changes, training, re-selection, fitted gains or November fitting. All outcomes offline; if zero usable examples, no metric.",
  "prior_use": "October 19/26 fit and October 30 design evaluation excluded. Frozen head trained on procedural geometries; bundled input scorecard and model/floor history came from previous development. November 9 crash/November 11 races, excerpts/tests, floor fitting, race maps or lines have prior analysis/overlap; all are descriptive only. No Nov 6 dependency. No rb2 Nov 16 driving bag included (line is not a run). Intake shared topic availability and top speeds before reservation, not frozen-policy errors. Configuration/hardware/course or indirect development overlap unresolved for Nov 16; call reserved, not independent. Never promote a run based on outcomes. Preserve any new provenance qualification.",
